From d1a9ae1fda71d86b31129ae42ea8387212fbc2be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:46:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: Backspace edits a text input on macOS too

Upstream compiles the Backspace arm out on macOS and leaves deleting to
an AppleStandardKeybinding("deleteBackward:") from Cocoa's text system.
A terminal host has no Cocoa text system and sends no keybindings, so in
hotty-blitz on macOS, Backspace in a text field did nothing (plexos
HOTTY-BACKSPACE-01). The arm now applies on every platform. A host that
sent the keybinding as well would delete twice; hotty-blitz's hosts send
none.
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/node/text.rs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/blitz-dom/src/node/text.rs b/packages/blitz-dom/src/node/text.rs
index 288f74aa..86c476ec 100644
--- a/packages/blitz-dom/src/node/text.rs
+++ b/packages/blitz-dom/src/node/text.rs
@@ -323,8 +323,8 @@ impl TextInputData {
                 return Some(GeneratedTextInputEvent::Input);
             }
 
-            // On macOS this is handled by the apple standard keybindings
-            #[cfg(not(target_os = "macos"))]
+            // On macOS too: a host without Cocoa's text system (a terminal)
+            // sends no "deleteBackward:" keybinding for Backspace.
             Key::Backspace => {
                 if action_mod {
                     driver.backdelete_word()
-- 
